+# SOCC log reader: preserved time labels and operational-record targets
+
+October30,2026. TEL02/TEL04, AUD016-A1, NI02/NI03 and TEL-NI-TIME. **A concrete public mirror of the AA SOC/SOCC log has been located and partially read.** It supplies exact page/Bates targets for the chronology referenced in interviews. This is a reader-level acquisition/read, not an authenticated native log, official release counterpart or completed call reconstruction.
+
+[Public log reader, document16762194](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-911-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version). The viewer advertises32 pages. The bibliography that pointed to it labels it as a January15,2002 SOCC chronology; the visible p3/p4 print label is **1/15/02 7:21**. That is not proof of native creation time or the exact version used at the November2003 interview. The source PDF was not downloaded; original byte count/hash remain **unknown**. The interface displayed a sign-up/free-trial download link; no download/login was attempted and no gate was bypassed.
+
+## Reading and provenance
+
+Inspected: p1's boxed scope and upper flight display; p3 status/header plus the complete lower chronology table/footer; p4 table/footer across upper/lower viewports; only the upper continuation on p32. **This is not a full32-page or complete four-page reading.** Advertisements temporarily obscured some viewports; normal zoom, page navigation and fullscreen were used to read the selected table regions. No hidden assets, document state, API, OCR text behind redactions or sign-in data were accessed.
+
+P1 identifies the record as selected information recorded by SOCC director/support, rather than all information. P3 is printed **3of32 / AA KEAN COMM002532**; p4 is **4of32 / AA KEAN COMM002533**. These two exact pages narrow the release/version request. Four inspected browser screenshots were saved locally with byte/hash pins. They are **browser-rendered JPEG derivatives**, not the source PDF or original page-image entities, and are excluded from publication. [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) preserves that distinction.
+
+## Time labels retained without filling gaps
+
+On p3, the first table row is **0740**, followed by **0738**, a Boston-call row with **no time in its own cell**, then **0744**. The first row reports an operations manager advising of a number1-flight-attendant call and an aircraft emergency;0738 concerns lockout;0744 concerns ATC treating the flight as a hijack. Do not silently reorder the rows or give the blank cell0738/0744.
+
+The [previously recovered official November19 interview](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialive/0/6096/2609600/content/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00014.pdf#page=2), p2, attributes **7:27CT** to a SOC timeline for the Gonzalez call, while p3 has **7:38CT** for lockout and **7:44CT** in the declaration context. Preserve the mirror's0740 and the interview's7:27 with their different descriptions; they have not been joined to one call/event or the same timeline version. **No13-minute actual delay or altered chronology is established.** A different report/event, entry-versus-event time, version difference or transcription problem remains an untested possibility. The exact FI log, source timeline and interview annotations would discriminate.
+
+Matching7:38/7:44 does not independently validate the interview, whose participants had a timeline before them. The prior **11:27/19:39 elapsed-position versus absolute/event-label questions remain unresolved**; this reading does not choose an anchor. The table's own clock definition has not been authenticated. P1 also contains a separate **0739 11Sep01** label and **11/1238Z** in flight information. Do not apply the interview's Central-Time convention to all display/table/print fields without their definitions.
+
+## Specific operational records to pursue
+
+- **0748, p3:** a request to contact FAA command center about removing or de-identifying Flight11 on ASD. This is evidence of a recorded request, not proof it was received or executed, what the display then showed, or why any later track existed. Seek request/receipt/action audit and display/feed records; technical interpretation stays with the technical investigation.
+- **0752, p3:** a reported drop/redial for a secure call. The November interview p4 separately describes an apparent tape-counter reset and second recording. These are separate candidate events until call identities and clocks join them. No missing segment or native continuity finding follows.
+- **0805 with parenthetical0745, p3:** lockout and earlier reported manager notification have distinct printed labels. Keep both rather than substituting one for the other.
+- **0822 /0905 /0916, p4:** unconfirmed United-aircraft reports and later identification are different knowledge states. They are not physical-impact times or proof nobody knew earlier.
+- **0833 /0846 /0936 /0941, p4:** reported ground-stop information, airline instruction, FAA presence and conference contact identify separate possible receipt/bridge/notification records. They do not prove a total FAA-contact blackout or authenticate completed deliveries.
+- **0834, p4:** the log contains a report attributing both WTC aircraft to American. Preserve it as a reported misidentification, not an accurate account of where Flight77 struck. This and the repeated unconfirmed reports are contrary evidence to treating every timeline entry as a precise, settled event.
+
+These are source-record and verification leads, not established concealment, deliberate warning suppression or conspiracy. Existing successful notifications, source uncertainty and mistaken reports remain alongside the concerns. [LEDGER.json](LEDGER.json), SL01-SL06, pins exact rows, preserves all10 printed time cells and two blanks in p3 order, and carries the missing inputs as TODOs.
+
+## Actual work and limits
+
+Four web query strings plus one prospectively declared official-catalog query were used. The official query displayed1,513 results; only the first20 titles were inspected, without confirming an exact original log object. The bibliography and public-reader routes were followed, with the additional reader navigation declared before use. No exhaustive search/absence claim, original PDF hash, native FI log, complete chronology/version chain or call/clock/audio test is claimed.
+
+[verify.py](verify.py) checks supplied screenshot identities and calculates the selected table's literal row-label ordering from the manual ledger. Its conditional numeric result is about document order, not elapsed event time or clock accuracy. [VERIFICATION.json](VERIFICATION.json) records the actual run. Manual reading is not independently replicated by checking our ledger. The prior November-unit29pass/1failed OCR result remains unchanged; it is not replaced by this different check.
+
+All18 five-track completion criteria remain open/partial, including the prioritized FAA correctedQFR/delivery, signed action/no-action and recommendation outcomes. Source data, private correspondence, raw images, full reader text/OCR, personnel/contact/account data and strategy are excluded from this seven-file public derivative. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) records the actual addition at a unique path; previous records are unchanged. Publication requires separate fresh AveLyra destination/identity/author+committer/ref and every-file verification and is not substantive goal completion.
